      "problem": "Given that $‖u‖=4$ and $u\\cdot v=-16$, find the smallest possible value of $‖2v‖.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-16| & \\le 4\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ 4 & \\le ‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the inequality by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 4 & \\le 2\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ 8 & \\le ‖2v‖\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $‖2v‖$ is $8.$",
